   "text": "routed experts 58×192 **15.33B** (61.0%) · attention ×61 **5.37B** (21.4%) · shared expert ×58 **1.92B** (7.6%) · dense FFN ×3 **906.0M** (3.6%) · lm head **1.54B** (6.1%) · embed **0** (row lookup) · routers + norms **69.2M** (0.3%)"
  },
  {
   "id": "cap-title",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -900,
   "y": -1300,
   "width": 1250,
   "height": 200,
   "text": "# K2-Horizon-375B-A23B — model  \nRead top → bottom, left column (L0–30) then right column (L31–60). **Grey bars = tensors**, length ∝ channels per token (0.08 px/channel). **Boxes = operations**, all the same size; where parameters and compute live is the pair of bars above. T = sequence length. *Layer* tab = one MoE layer in detail."
  },
  {
   "id": "cap-legend",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 450,
   "y": -1300,
   "width": 1250,
   "height": 200,
   "text": "Layer rows — **dense**: SwiGLU FFN 6144→16384→6144 (L0–2, `mlp_only_layers`) · **MoE**: sigmoid router picks 8 of 192 experts (6144→1792→6144) + 1 always-on shared expert.    \nEvery layer has the same attention: plain GQA, 48 query / 8 KV heads × 128, RoPE on 64 of 128 dims, full causal over 524,288 tokens (no sliding window, no MLA, no linear attention).    \nStored **379.17B** (376.09B without embed + head ≈ the name's 375B); active **25.13B** per token (23.59B without lm head ≈ the name's A23B)."
  },
  {
